      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking high-potency vitamin K supplements while on warfarin is dangerous because it can interfere with the blood thinner's ability to prevent clots. Warfarin works by blocking vitamin K, so adding extra vitamin K can cause your blood to clot too quickly, leading to serious stroke or bleeding risks. Please stop taking the supplements immediately and contact your cardiologist today to review your dosage and adjust your treatment plan safely. Do not continue this regimen until a healthcare professional gives you specific advice based on your recent blood work.",
