      "content": "While vitamin K is a natural nutrient essential for bone health, the interaction between specific high-dose supplements and warfarin is a critical medical issue that cannot be treated casually. Warfarin requires a very narrow and inconsistent baseline of vitamin K in your body to work correctly, meaning even small doses from supplements can drastically alter your clotting factors and cause life-threatening complications. Because your doctor prescribed a medication specifically targeted to inhibit vitamin K, he was anticipating you might be taking these supplements or should have discussed any other source of vitamin K with him in advance. Please do not take any more supplements and call your cardiologist or pharmacist immediately for urgent guidance to ensure your safety.",
